he daughter grew up to be a beautiful woman. A dragon appeared, causing a flood in the village. The daughter possessed an incredible power, suppressing the dragon's movements. However, she did not completely eliminate the dragon, so the flood continued every four years. [5] The daughter's strength and beauty were highly praised. Shortly thereafter, numerous people from all over the world came to ask for her hand in marriage after hearing the legend. The daughter gave them a challenge, saying she would choose a husband who held the Penglai zither. However, no one succeeded. Although there were those who brought counterfeit instruments, the daughter's touch immediately broke the strings. However, a man from the east overcame great difficulties and finally succeeded. The daughter married him as promised. [6] Soon after, the couple had a daughter, named Qiyao. Qiyao grew up and possessed even greater power than her mother. When the dragon returned, Qiyao played the Penglai zither, and the sound of the zither cut off the dragon's head, neatly eliminating the dragon. At the same time, the Penglai zither that had fulfilled its mission was broken into two pieces. [7] The villagers were surprised and asked the daughter why she could accomplish what her mother could not. The mother answered that although she inherited a large amount of power from the gods, it was not enough to eliminate another god. It was only because Qiyao mixed excellent human blood that she could eliminate the dragon. Although Qiyao only inherited half of her mother's power, she inherited her father's entire power. To eliminate the dragon, the power of the gods and human power were both necessary. [8] At the age of forty, Qiyao passed her title to her daughter and descended to become an ordinary person. The daughter also inherited half of her mother's power and all of human power. Although Qiyao had a son, he could only inherit half of his mother's power and not his father's, so he could not succeed Qiyao